# nr-workbench project
#
# The rule: small provenance records are tracked, large payloads are not. The
# repository should still be able to say what happened even when the data is
# absent from this machine.

# --- Payloads: large, reproducible from the instrument ---------------------
samples/*/data/raw/
*.nxs
*.nxs.h5
*.h5

# Fit payloads: DREAM chains and large bitmaps. The manifests, parameter
# tables and SVG figures beside them ARE tracked.
samples/*/results/*/fit/*.mc.gz
samples/*/results/*/fit/*.mcmc
samples/*/results/*/fit/*.chain
samples/*/results/*/output/
*.png

# AuRE scouting runs. The setup and the physics knobs it ran under ARE tracked
# -- they are small, and together they say what was asked for. Everything under
# output/ is not, for two reasons beyond size: AuRE resolves data files to
# ABSOLUTE paths and writes them into final_state.json, and that file also
# carries the full prompt/response transcript of the run. Both are exactly what
# the rules above keep out of a directory that gets shared and archived.
#
# Nothing is lost. The durable record of an AuRE run is the model spec
# `nrw aure import` writes, which IS committed and names the AuRE version and
# commit that proposed it.
samples/*/aure/*/output/

# --- Machine-local state ---------------------------------------------------
.nrw/cache/
.nrw/backups/
.nrw/lock

# Where `nrw` lives on *this* machine. These files name an absolute path, which
# is exactly what must not be committed -- and the right answer differs per
# machine anyway, so a shared copy would be wrong for everyone but its author.
#
# Listed for every harness this package knows, not just the ones this project
# uses: ignoring a path that is never written costs nothing, and a line that
# only appears once someone adds a harness is a line that gets forgotten.
.nrw/bin/
.claude/settings.local.json
.opencode/local.json

# Unattended-session prompts and transcripts. A transcript is the whole tool
# stream of a session -- every file it read and every command output it saw --
# so it can contain anything that was on screen, including a key printed by
# something it ran. These directories get shared and archived; keep it out.
.nrw/agent/

# Refused-overwrite copies written by `nrw init` when a file has been edited.
# Review them, then merge or delete; never commit them.
*.nrw-new

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Credentials. An LLM API key in a beamtime repository is a real problem:
# these directories get shared, archived and published.
.env
.envrc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Explicitly tracked, despite looking like build output -----------------
# The provenance skeleton. Do not add these to the ignore list.
!.nrw/index.jsonl
!.nrw/schema/
!.nrw/scaffold.lock.json
!.nrw/skills.lock.json
!samples/*/results/*/manifest.json
!samples/*/results/*/figures/*.svg
